WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:04.560
They say Californians are
living the dream. - But things
aren't all back glamorous.

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:05.430
Nope.

00:00:05.430 --> 00:00:06.630
We have our struggles.

00:00:08.530 --> 00:00:09.700
It's no cakewalk.

00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:10.840
No kidding.

00:00:10.840 --> 00:00:12.160
For well over a century,

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:15.210
California was synonymous
with the American dream

00:00:15.210 --> 00:00:17.550
of starting over and making it big.

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:19.420
By the early 1960s,

00:00:19.420 --> 00:00:22.270
it had become the most
populous state in the country.

00:00:22.270 --> 00:00:24.590
Now, California's population is declining

00:00:24.590 --> 00:00:27.510
for the first time in recorded history.

00:00:27.510 --> 00:00:31.120
Like New York, Illinois,
Pennsylvania, Ohio,

00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:33.300
Michigan, and West Virginia,

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:35.850
California is losing a congressional seat,

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:38.320
another first for the Golden State.

00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:40.920
The reasons behind California's decline

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:42.210
aren't hard to fathom.

00:00:42.210 --> 00:00:44.500
According to Chief Executive magazine,

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:47.230
California is the worst
state to do business in,

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:51.080
a position at is held for
most of the list's existence.

00:00:51.080 --> 00:00:53.470
California ranks eighth in combined state

00:00:53.470 --> 00:00:55.200
and local tax burden,

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:57.820
forcing residents to
kick in an effective rate

00:00:57.820 --> 00:01:02.590
of 11.5 percent of their
income just for being alive.

00:01:02.590 --> 00:01:04.400
What do they get in return?

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:07.300
Public schools that rank
37th in the country,

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:09.390
insanely expensive housing

00:01:09.390 --> 00:01:11.770
whose costs are inflated
by strict environmental

00:01:11.770 --> 00:01:15.210
and land use regulations that
make it nearly impossible

00:01:15.210 --> 00:01:17.280
to match supply with demand.

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:19.450
Rolling blackouts and power shortages

00:01:19.450 --> 00:01:21.060
caused by environmental mandates

00:01:21.060 --> 00:01:23.400
and poor utility governance,

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:26.000
an above average violent crime rate,

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:28.670
and the nation's highest poverty rate

00:01:28.670 --> 00:01:32.330
with more than 36% of
California's residents

00:01:32.330 --> 00:01:35.200
at or near the poverty level.

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:38.470
Governor Gavin Newsom faces a
recall election in the fall,

00:01:38.470 --> 00:01:40.060
partly due to his hypocrisy

00:01:40.060 --> 00:01:42.560
regarding his own
stringent lockdown rules.

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:45.830
Rather than grapple with
his state sinking status,

00:01:45.830 --> 00:01:48.500
he's chosen instead to deny reality.

00:01:48.500 --> 00:01:52.070
This remarkable, remarkable home

00:01:52.070 --> 00:01:56.180
to more dreamers and doers than
any other part of the globe.

00:01:56.180 --> 00:01:58.570
A smarter strategy might be to look

00:01:58.570 --> 00:02:01.790
at the two biggest states
that are gaining in population

00:02:01.790 --> 00:02:03.440
at California's expense.

00:02:03.440 --> 00:02:08.440
Between 2010 and 2020, Florida's
population grew by 14.6 percent

00:02:09.630 --> 00:02:13.710
and Texas' increased by 15.9 percent.

00:02:13.710 --> 00:02:16.520
Their weather is awful
by California standards

00:02:16.520 --> 00:02:18.430
and they lack its natural beauty,

00:02:18.430 --> 00:02:21.530
but they ranked second and
first in business climate,

00:02:21.530 --> 00:02:23.550
which means more opportunity,

00:02:23.550 --> 00:02:27.360
even as their cost of living
is a fraction of California's.

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:31.330
Until and unless the Golden
State makes itself affordable

00:02:31.330 --> 00:02:32.900
to dreamers and doers,

00:02:32.900 --> 00:02:35.370
they'll keep heading
to other destinations.

00:02:35.370 --> 00:02:38.090
As California loses a congressional seat,

00:02:38.090 --> 00:02:40.120
Texas is picking up two.

00:02:40.120 --> 00:02:42.090
And demographers predict
that it may become

00:02:42.090 --> 00:02:44.850
the most populous state by 2045,

00:02:44.850 --> 00:02:48.100
much sooner than was predicted
just a few years ago.

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:51.380
Texas may not have the
beaches, the forests,

00:02:51.380 --> 00:02:53.340
the celebrities, or the glamour.

00:02:53.340 --> 00:02:56.210
It'll just have the jobs, the companies,

00:02:56.210 --> 00:02:58.543
the forward momentum, and the people.

